  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Early Recovery Response_Sindh &amp; Balochistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aim of the Project is building resilience of flood affected population of Taluka Faiz Gunj in district Khairpurmirus Sindh through restoration of Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), FES with safety and dignity. Under WASH sector 25920 (5082 families ) access to safe drinking water, sanitation and hygiene facilities. Under Food &amp; Economic Security (FES) the aim is to deliver lifesaving and livelihoods assistance for 7,063 flood affected most vulnerable people (1308 families) and under Protection it will restore conditions of safety and dignity, ensuring communities access to urgently needed assistance and protection and ability to participate meaningfully in the decisions that impact their lives.</narrative>
  </description>
